Files: models/face_detection_yunet_2026may.onnx
Copyright: 2023-2026 Shiqi Yu and contributors
           2023-2026 OpenCV Zoo contributors
License: Expat
Comment: YuNet face detector, distributed by the OpenCV Zoo under an explicit
 per-model licence beside the weights. Detection and five landmarks; ~230 KB.

Files: models/face_recognition_sface_2021dec.onnx
Copyright: 2021 Yaoyao Zhong and contributors
           2021-2026 OpenCV Zoo contributors
License: Apache-2.0
Comment: SFace, 128-dimension embedding, ~37 MB. The OpenCV Zoo ships a
 per-model Apache-2.0 LICENSE beside the ONNX, which is a grant on the artefact
 rather than an inference from a repository root.
 .
 One residual question is recorded here rather than hidden: the upstream
 zhongyy/SFace repository declares no licence, and neither the zoo model card
 nor the paper states the training dataset in terms that settle whether the
 redistributor had the right to grant Apache-2.0 over the weights. Face
 recognition models are commonly trained on CASIA-WebFace or MS-Celeb-1M, both
 research-only. This must be resolved before any Debian ITP. If it does not
 clear, the fallback is dlib's dlib_face_recognition_resnet_model_v1, which is
 CC0. See models/README.md.

Files: vendor/*
Copyright: the respective crate authors
License: Expat or Apache-2.0 or other-permissive
Comment: Launchpad's build machines have no network, so the Rust dependency
 tree is vendored into the source package. All 156 crates are permissively
 licensed and every one of them is compatible with GPL-3.0-or-later:
 .
   MIT and/or Apache-2.0 (dual)   152 crates
   BSD-3-Clause                   subtle, bindgen
   Zlib                           foldhash
   ISC                            libloading
   MPL-2.0                        dyn-eq
 .
 Each crate carries its own licence text in its vendored directory. This
 blanket stanza is adequate for a PPA and is NOT adequate for the Debian
 archive, which wants either per-crate librust-*-dev source packages or an
 explicit vendoring exception with a per-file audit.

